& [Requirements]
  + [COCD-001] add exact cantord invocation check-config plus one absolute service-config path while preserving the existing config server invocation unchanged
  + [COCD-002] check-config never binds a listener enters the service loop connects to a socket creates a process or contacts a provider
  + [COCD-003] reuse load_service_config unchanged for strict schema loopback bounds canonical authority paths and collision validation
  + [COCD-004] reuse SecretToken validation unchanged in memory and never serialize token bytes normalized token hash token length or token path
  + [COCD-005] reuse load_generation unchanged for activation schema sequence environment containment digest signed-environment preflight and PreparedRuntime construction
  + [COCD-006] define profile cantor-operator-configuration-diagnostic/0.1 with closed ready or refused status
  + [COCD-007] record an ordered prefix of exactly service_config authentication_token and activation_environment checks with passed or refused status
  + [COCD-008] on ready report only safe schema listener family and port resource limits active binding prepared-runtime metrics and ordered package count
  + [COCD-009] on refusal report exactly one public code stage subject and closed guidance string without the raw ServiceFault message
  + [COCD-010] report a bounded config-file SHA256 only when the config bytes can be read within the existing 64 KiB limit and never report its path or content
  + [COCD-011] always publish explicit false privacy/effect claims for paths token content token hash config content activation content environment content listener binding service start provider contact and remote access
  + [COCD-012] require ready to have summary and no fault and refused to have one fault and no summary
  + [COCD-013] emit exactly one compact JSON object and newline on stdout with no domain-refusal diagnostic on stderr
  + [COCD-014] exit zero for ready three for refused two for invalid invocation and seventy for stdout serialization failure
  + [COCD-015] repeat the same admitted files to obtain byte-identical diagnostic JSON
  + [COCD-016] prove ready configuration invalid strict JSON nonloopback token activation digest path containment and CLI invocation cases
  + [COCD-017] adversarially prove serialized ready and refused forms contain neither fixture root token text authority filenames nor raw environment source text
  + [COCD-018] retain one provider-free checked ready report and one sanitized refused report plus independent verifier and evidence manifest
  + [COCD-019] update resident-service and product-readiness documentation while leaving configuration generation secret provisioning repair migration and operator acceptance open
  + [COCD-020] after implementation publication regenerate and verify the deterministic portable bundle against the new exact cantord binary and published source commit
  + [COCD-021] pass focused debug and release tests warnings-denied Clippy format workspace recursive evidence attribution commit push and post-push gates
  + [COCD-022] never download dependencies install mutate operator inputs create secrets start a service contact provider or remote hosts persist effects use FPGA or enter Minecraft scope

